        },
        {
          "concern": "An OAuth prompt still appears after restart on O365 despite the order fix; later ESR uplift and backout change the release outcome.",
          "response": "The main bug reopens after an O365 report and links1912556 as the additional fix. Uplift approval is temporarily reset, then ESR128.2.2 lands and128.2.3 backs it out. Later the author marks central-landed work fixed while keeping the ESR problem to be solved in a combined patch.",
          "applied": "The selected655 diff only fixes stored-token lookup order. It does not include the Microsoft normalization or broader persistence work in674. The shared token-set contract remains valid source evidence despite the distinct release history.",
          "outcome": "Central FIXED status is not a claim that every ESR channel or provider prompt was resolved. Historical manual-testing, Gmail support links and reported backout are retained; linked support pages and jobs remain unread."
